## `true` si el tipo es un primitivo.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave is_base with t as ref to SemaTypeTable, id as int into bool:
    return (calling at with t, id).kind == tk.SemaTypeKind.TkBase

## `true` si el tipo es `TkError`.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave is_error with t as ref to SemaTypeTable, id as int into bool:
    return id <= 0 or (calling at with t, id).kind == tk.SemaTypeKind.TkError

## ¿Un valor por defecto plegado (`DEF_*`) encaja con el tipo del parámetro?
##
## Los primitivos se comparan por nombre canónico; runas, omens, genéricos y
## alias se dejan a la llamada (C hace la conversión).
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave default_fits with t as ref to SemaTypeTable, pty as int, dkind as int into bool:
    if pty <= 0:
        return true
    var ty as tk.SemaType is calling at with t, pty
    if ty.kind != tk.SemaTypeKind.TkBase:
        return true
    var name as string is calling npool.text with t->names, ty.name
    var numeric as bool is name == "int" or name == "i8" or name == "i16" or name == "i32" or name == "i64" or name == "u8" or name == "u16" or name == "u32" or name == "u64" or name == "usize" or name == "isize" or name == "float" or name == "f32" or name == "f64" or name == "char"
    if dkind == DEF_INT or dkind == DEF_CHAR or dkind == DEF_FLOAT:
        return numeric
    if dkind == DEF_BOOL:
        return name == "bool"
    if dkind == DEF_STRING:
        return name == "string"
    return false
